  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/41264179625524953342">
    <nyt:search_api_query rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://api.nytimes.com/svc/search/v1/article?query=+nytd_org_facet%3A%5BMorgan+Stanley%5D&amp;rank=newest&amp;fields=abstract,author,body,byline,classifiers_facet,column_facet,date,day_of_week_facet,des_facet,desk_facet,fee,geo_facet,lead_paragraph,material_type_facet,multimedia,nytd_byline,nytd_des_facet,nytd_geo_facet,nytd_lead_paragraph,nytd_org_facet,nytd_per_facet,nytd_section_facet,nytd_title,nytd_works_mentioned_facet,org_facet,page_facet,per_facet,publication_day,publication_month,publication_year,section_page_facet,small_image_height,small_image_url,small_image_width,source_facet,title,url,word_count,works_mentioned_facet</nyt:search_api_query>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-19</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/news/business/companies/morgan_stanley/index.html"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2006-07-21</nyt:first_use>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.morgan_stanley"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_org"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Oct. 21, 2009
Morgan Stanley traces its roots back to the House of Morgan, the grandest name on Wall Street. But its last decade of operation has been one of recurrent turmoil, and in the last year, the credit crisis has toppled Morgan from its standing as a premier investment bank.
John J. Mack took the helm at Morgan in 2005, when the company was demoralized after a controversial merger with the retail brokerage firm Dean Witter. Mr. Mack was lauded for revitalizing the firm, but he encouraged a newly aggressive attitude toward trading. Mr. Mack said often and publicly, from his first days as chief executive, that the firm would deploy its own capital more aggressively and enter higher-growth and riskier areas like mortgages and leveraged loans. As a result, Mr. Mack laid the groundwork for the firm's trouble when the subprime mortgage market collapsed last year.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">139</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Morgan Stanley</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/morgan_stanley_org"/>
  </rdf:Description>
