  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N60839309888659393262">
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">6</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">European Aeronautic Defense and Space Co</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/news/business/companies/european_aeronautic_defence_and_space_company_eads/index.html"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-18</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:search_api_query rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://api.nytimes.com/svc/search/v1/article?query=+nytd_org_facet%3A%5BEuropean+Aeronautic+Defense+and+Space+Co%5D&amp;rank=newest&amp;fields=abstract,author,body,byline,classifiers_facet,column_facet,date,day_of_week_facet,des_facet,desk_facet,fee,geo_facet,lead_paragraph,material_type_facet,multimedia,nytd_byline,nytd_des_facet,nytd_geo_facet,nytd_lead_paragraph,nytd_org_facet,nytd_per_facet,nytd_section_facet,nytd_title,nytd_works_mentioned_facet,org_facet,page_facet,per_facet,publication_day,publication_month,publication_year,section_page_facet,small_image_height,small_image_url,small_image_width,source_facet,title,url,word_count,works_mentioned_facet</nyt:search_api_query>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_org"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 6, 2009
EADS is formally known as the European Aeronautic Defence and Space Company. It returned to profit in 2008, helped by a record year for aircraft deliveries at its Airbus subsidiary, but anxieties about the future of its military transport plane and the financial crisis rattling its customers will be primary concerns for the company in 2009.
Airbus, which took over the military aircraft division of EADS on Jan. 1, has inherited the troubled A400M military transport plane, which is fast becoming its most pressing concern. The aircraft failed to meet its first-flight deadline of March 31, 2009, because of engine-related software problems. But termination is considered unlikely, and France, Germany and Spain have already expressed a desire to negotiate.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/european_aeronautic_defense_and_space_co_org"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.eads"/>
