  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/66182674496565277792">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The New York Giants’ 2008 season ended in stark contrast to the 2007 campaign, which concluded with an unlikely Super Bowl victory over the previously unbeaten New England Patriots. After breezing through the first 12 games of the regular season, losing only once, the Giants lost three of their last four games to finish with a 12-4 record, but earned the number one seed in the National Football Conference, home-field advantage in the playoffs and a first-round bye. In the divisional-round game, the Giants were eliminated when they fell to the Philadelphia Eagles, 23-11.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">3</nyt:number_of_variants>
