  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/78408960637253476022">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en"> "Some read it and like it. Some read it and don't like it. But everybody reads it."
That assessment of The New York Times came in 1980 from former President Richard M. Nixon, who no doubt counted himself in the second camp. (His Justice Department tried to restrain The Times in 1971 from publishing the Pentagon Papers, a secret official history of the Vietnam War. The Times -- and newspapers generally -- won a vital legal battle when the Supreme Court ruled that the government's effort at prior restraint was unconstitutional.)</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/organizations/n/newyorktimes_the/index.html"/>
