  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N29184897019644128492">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Seattle Post-Intelligencer published its last printed edition on March 17, 2009, which made it the largest American newspaper to become an Internet-only news source. The daily paper was established in 1863.
The P-I was afflicted by the falling revenues affecting the entire industry. It lost $14 million in 2008, and the Hearst Corporation, its owner, announced in January 2009 that it would cease printing unless it found a buyer.
The P-I continues to exist as a Web site, a transformation that might hint at a path for future newspaper closings.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">3</nyt:number_of_variants>
