    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">After more than a decade of sensational buzz, Starbucks is struggling nationwide as it faces slowing sales growth and increased competition.
The man who built the chain, Howard D. Schultz, has retaken the reins in an effort to revive it. Mr. Schultz has said he wants to refocus on the â€œcustomer experience,â€ recapturing some of the magic of the chainâ€™s early years, when employees â€” who had heard the term barista before Starbucks came along? â€” made the drinks by hand and customers were excited by top-notch coffee.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_org"/>
