  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/79087909181639884802">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: July 30, 2009
, ETA has killed more than 825 people in recent decades in its campaign for an independent Basque homeland. European Union ETA, is a militant separatist organization founded in 1959 with the goal of establishing an independent Basque state encompassing sections of northern Spain and southern France. Considered a terrorist group by the United States State Department and the   Euskadi Ta Askatasuna ("Basque Homeland and Freedom"), or
After one of its members fatally shot a Civil Guard officer in 1968, the group's attacks over the years killed scores, including nearly 350 civilians, according to figures from the Spanish Interior Ministry. The attacks have included assassinations of politicians, car bombs placed outside police stations and indiscriminate bombings in parks and shopping centers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_org"/>
