  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N83010763078989389452">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 20, 2009
The Huffington Post, the news Web site, evolved from a collective of celebrity bloggers recruited by Arianna Huffington, the columnist and onetime candidate for governor of California.
Introduced in May 2005, Ms. Huffington lined up more than 250 of what she called "the most creative minds" in the country to write a group blog ranging from politics and entertainment to sports and religion. Contributors included the retired anchorman Walter Cronkite, the former Bush speechwriter David Frum, the actress Diane Keaton and the lawyer Vernon E. Jordan Jr.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Huffington Post</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.the_huffington_post"/>
