    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">African National Congress</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated April 29, 2009
The African National Congress led the South African liberation from apartheid, and has dominated the country's politics in the years since. The political party has won every election since the end of apartheid with overwhelming support, turning South Africa into a virtual one-party state.
In April 2009 the party, led by its leader Jacob G. Zuma, won its fourth consecutive electoral victory. Parliament elects the president, but the A.N.C.'s dominance assures that Mr. Zuma will take the oath of office on May 9.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-09-08</nyt:first_use>
