    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Oct. 29, 2009
The United Federation of Teachers is New York City's teachers' union, and one of the most powerful labor unions in the country. The union has had a pretty good relationship with Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg since he took office in 2002.
of the A.F.T. in 2008. elected president , who served as the U.F.T.'s president for 10 years, was  Randi Weingarten .  American Federation of Teachers , both of whom went on to become president of the U.F.T.'s national parent union, the  Sandra Feldman  and  Albert Shanker The union's presidency has been filled by labor giants</skos:definition>
