  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/74336341705779880702">
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_org"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: May 19, 2009
In August 2002, the Bay Area Laboratory Co-Operative became the focus of an investigation by an I.R.S. agent, Jeff Novitzky, who had received a tip that company was selling more than just supplements and vitamins to elite athletes.
In 2006, Patrick Arnold, the Balco chemist who created the undetectable designer steroid called "the clear," pleaded guilty to conspiracy to distribute steroids. He received a sentence of three months in prison.  Based on the testimony from many of the athletes, Conte and Anderson accepted plea agreements from the government in 2005 on charges they distributed steroids and laundered money to avoid significant time in jail. Conte received a sentence of four months in jail, Anderson received a sentence of three months. Also that year, James Valente, the vice president of Balco, and Remi Korchemny, a track coach affiliated with Balco, pleaded guilty to distributing banned substances and received probation.  After Anderson and Conte refused to cooperate with the investigation, prosecutors convened a grand jury to begin hearing evidence from Balco's clients. The list of athletes summoned before the grand jury were some of the most high profile ones in sports -- Marion Jones, Tim Montgomery, Jason Giambi, Gary Sheffield and Bonds.  In September 2003, Novitzky and a team of federal agents raided Balco's office, which was located in the agent's hometown of Burlingame, Calif. The agents also raided the home of Barry Bonds's trainer, Greg Anderson, and a storage unit owned by Balco's president and founder, Victor Conte. Late at night, Novitzky rummaged through Balco's trash, finding drug samples and financial records that identified famous athletes in baseball, track and field and football who were receiving performance-enhancing drugs.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-02-27</nyt:latest_use>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.bay_area_laboratory_co-operative"/>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">58</nyt:associated_article_count>
