    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 21, 2009
Oracle, which is based in Redwood City, Calif., is one of the world's largest software companies.
was doing pioneering research on the subject, but doubted relational databases were commercially viable. Mr. Ellison put together a prototype and made his first sale to the Central Intelligence Agency. I.B.M. Lawrence J. Ellison founded it in 1977 while working for a data storage company. All that he needed to go into business was a product. He stumbled on relational database theory, which held that if data could be stored in computers in a less ''hierarchical'' way, it would be easier to find and use.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
