  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N82709777299500467192">
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">YouTube.com</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">3</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/youtube_com_org"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 17, 2009
YouTube is far and away the most popular destination on the Internet for viewing video, most of which has been posted by users. Nearly two-thirds of all video views in the United States occur on YouTube, according to the measurement firm Nielsen. In March 2009, the site had more than 90 million visitors, 10 times as many as the next biggest site.
Still, YouTube's owner, Google, which paid $1.65 billion for the site in October 2006, has struggled to make it profitable.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">353</nyt:associated_article_count>
