    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Whitney Museum of American Art</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Whitney Museum of American Art, founded in 1931 by Gertrude Vanderbilt Whitney, originally in a building connected to her home in Greenwich Village, owns one of the world's major collections of 20th-century American art. Today, in a blocky granite building on Madison Avenue designed by Marcel Breuer and completed in 1966, the museum owns some 12,000 works: paintings, sculptures, drawings, prints, photographs and multimedia. Works from the permanent collection, dated 1900 to 1949, are shown on the museum's fifth floor; art from 1950 to the present is on the second floor.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/organizations/w/whitney_museum_of_american_art/index.html"/>
