    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: March 11, 2009
. This long-running Philadephia hip-hop outfit -- "the legendary Roots crew" is how they're introduced each night -- hasn't historically been known for humor. But like many others in these lean times, the band is adapting. NBC " on  Jimmy Fallon The Roots rule the musical roost at "Late Night With
perhaps pretended not to notice when she emerged in a skin-tight black dress to the thump of E.U.'s go-go classic "Da Butt." Serena Williams 's "C.R.E.A.M." (as in, "cash rules everything around me"), and  Wu-Tang Clan  appeared on the show in early March, the band serenaded him with  Donald Trump When</skos:definition>
